{"created": "2026-10-19T03:28:26.405473+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-19T03:28:26.841749+00:00", "id": 23463481, "conceptrecid": "23463480", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23463480", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "metadata": {"title": "Packing n\u00b2 \u2212 n + 1 unit squares in a square of side less than n, for every n \u2265 15", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "publication_date": "2026-10-18", "description": "<p>Let s(N) be the smallest side of a square containing N unit squares with disjoint interiors, rotations allowed. We prove s(n\u00b2 \u2212 n + 1) &lt; n for every integer n \u2265 15. More generally, n\u00b2 \u2212 n + 1 + p + 2q unit squares fit below side n whenever p, q \u2265 0 are integers and 16p + 21q \u2264 n \u2212 15. The proof iterates the four-piece construction of Arslanov, Mustafin and Shangitbayev, using known and new base packings and exact rational packings of 257 squares in 17 \u00d7 16 and 443 squares in 22 \u00d7 21. Independently written exact programs check the finite inputs, and we supply generated certificates for 15 \u2264 n \u2264 64. Lean 4 formalises the first theorem and the two unmixed bounds, including kernel checks of all 18 input pieces. The contribution is an explicit threshold and construction, rather than a new asymptotic waste bound.</p><p>Files: the note as PDF (draft v0.9, 7 pages) and its LaTeX source. Exact certificates and checkers: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-certs\">squarepack-certs</a>, commit 078789a4cfd36f915f1bfbe76d742413d79b2965. Lean 4 formalisation: <a href=\"https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-lean\">squarepack-lean</a>, commit 947bdae.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Fang, Kevin", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["square packing", "unit squares", "Erd\u0151s\u2013Graham", "combinatorial geometry", "Lean 4", "formal verification", "exact certificates"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-certs/tree/078789a4cfd36f915f1bfbe76d742413d79b2965", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/TheSnakeFang/squarepack-lean/tree/947bdae", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://jlevy.github.io/squares/result/t-163.html", "relation": "isReviewedBy", "resource_type": "other", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "0.9", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23463480"}}]}}, "title": "Packing n\u00b2 \u2212 n + 1 unit squares in a square of side less than n, for every n \u2265 15", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23463481", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23463481", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23463481?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23463481", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23463481/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23463480", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23463480", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23463480", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23463480", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23463481/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23463481/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23463481/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23463481/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23463481:fang-2026-n2-n-1.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23463481:fang-2026-n2-n-1.pdf/full/%5